= The Generals' Republic

The general strike did not bring Kapp down. His men sit in the ministries, and the army has decided it likes them better than it liked the Republic. Lüttwitz's decrees dissolve the councils and put the unions under military supervision. The Social Democratic ministers have gone from Stuttgart to Switzerland. The special courts sentence our people by the hundred.

There will be no elections. [? if e23_red_refuge = 1 : One corner of Germany is still in the workers' hands, behind its own front line. ?][? if e23_red_refuge = 0 : There is nowhere in Germany the regime does not reach. ?]

- @underground: Go underground everywhere.
- @refuge: Take the Zentrale to the red region.

@underground
subtitle: The party becomes a conspiracy, for years.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 3;
!}

The Zentrale disappears into cellars and safe flats. Its next full meeting is held in Prague.

- @end: See how it ends.

@refuge
subtitle: The red region becomes the base of what is left of the German revolution.
view-if: e23_red_refuge = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 2;
!}

The Zentrale, its archive and its best organisers cross the lines at night in a lorry full of potatoes.

- @end: See how it ends.

@end
go-to: game_over
